<title>USA: Franklin Electronic buys Belgian firm.</title>
<headline>Franklin Electronic buys Belgian firm.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, N.J. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franklin Electronic Publishers Inc said Tuesday it completed its acquisition of privately-held Advanced Data Management Group SA of Wavre, Belgium.</p>
<p>A company spokesman declined to say how much Franklin paid for the electronic book distributor, but said he thought it was &quot;fairly minimal.&quot;</p>
<p>Franklin said Advanced Data distributes Franklin products and other brands in the Netherlands, Belgium and Luxembourg. Franklin's stock traded unchanged at 9-3/4 Tuesday afternoon, close to its 52-week low of 9-3/8.</p>
